WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:01.201
Notable developments

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.402
in the special counsel's

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:04.371
investigation of Donald Trump,

00:00:04.371 --> 00:00:05.972
including word of yet

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:07.007
another subpoena

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:08.008
involving the former

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:09.776
president's finances.

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:11.044
According to notes that Evan

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:12.879
Corcoran took of his conversations

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:13.880
with his client.

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.849
Donald Trump, the former president,

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:17.917
wanted to fight the subpoena

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:18.651
that demanded

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:19.486
that he return

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:21.821
classified documents that he had no right

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:23.823
to have after his time in office.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.558
Now, these notes taken

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:27.394
by Corcoran are providing

00:00:27.394 --> 00:00:29.362
more insight into Trump's thinking

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:30.530
and his actions

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:31.598
around the time

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:33.800
the criminal investigation was launched.

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:34.868
And now

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:35.368
they sit

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:37.170
in the hands of the special counsel,

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:38.304
Jack Smith.

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:39.973
Joining us now is John Dean.

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:40.740
He was the White House

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.542
counsel for Richard Nixon.

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:45.245
And just like Evan Corcoran, John,

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:46.546
you testified

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:48.715
about your conversations with

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:49.949
President Nixon. So

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:52.485
as you listen to

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:54.721
what has been reported here in your mind,

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:56.689
why would there even be

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:59.859
dozens of pages of documents notes about

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:02.962
what to do with a lawful subpoena?

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:03.296
Shouldn't

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:04.164
that conversation

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:04.898
between attorney

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:07.734
and client be pretty short?

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:08.435
Well, I know Mr.

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:09.335
Trump in the past

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:09.702
has said

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:10.670
he was surprised

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:11.438
when his White House

00:01:11.438 --> 00:01:13.973
counsel were keeping notes.

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:15.008
I didn't keep notes

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:17.610
when I was White House counsel,

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:18.244
and I didn't know

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:19.345
there was a taping system,

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.114
which fortunately was there.

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:23.650
But the immediate problem for

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:26.653
Evan Cochran is that he,

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:30.023
I think, did suspect that his client

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:31.257
was a little squirrely

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:32.192
and he didn't know

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:33.526
how things were going to turn out.

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:35.428
So he kept very detailed notes,

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:37.997
apparently down to as reported.

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:40.300
Such things as his facial expressions

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.401
during conversation.

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:42.836
Yeah.

00:01:42.836 --> 00:01:43.837
I mean, it does seem to

00:01:43.837 --> 00:01:46.039
suggest that Corcoran

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:47.774
had a sense that something was

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:49.876
was potentially going to come back

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:52.612
to and needed to be documented.

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:53.947
One of the sources

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:55.748
described Corcoran's notes

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:58.017
as, quote, overly detailed

00:01:58.017 --> 00:01:59.152
Another source said

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:00.553
that some were surprised

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:02.722
that at that level of detail,

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:04.190
do you think that Corcoran

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:05.158
could have also been

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:07.660
trying to perhaps protect himself

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:11.297
I think there's a good reason to suspect

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:12.198
that's the case.

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:13.833
I think there's a

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:15.235
we don't know what's in the notes

00:02:15.235 --> 00:02:15.902
at this point.

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:17.270
We know they are

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:20.940
where valuable enough to the prosecutors

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.442
that they went to court

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:24.844
and got a judge to say that.

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:26.513
It appears

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:27.780
that they're certainly evidence

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.816
to indicate that Mr.

00:02:29.816 --> 00:02:31.351
Cochran's client, the president

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:32.986
or the former president,

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:34.120
was taking advantage

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:36.122
of that counsel to commit a crime.

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:37.891
And that's the exception

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:39.626
Which is breaching the privilege

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:41.794
which judges don't like to do.

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:43.530
That's a very sacred privilege.

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:46.266
So judges are very aware of it.

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:46.866
And it's a

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:48.067
But it's

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.536
very telling to us

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:51.871
as spectators in this this point

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:53.940
that we are seeing a case

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.675
that is being built

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:57.243
and there's judges

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:59.012
who are looking at this evidence,

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:02.115
see evidence of criminal behavior by Mr.

00:03:02.115 --> 00:03:02.615
Trump.

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:04.651
Yeah, that crime fraud exception

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:06.452
was found by the judge in this case,

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:08.922
which is a very high bar typically.

00:03:08.922 --> 00:03:11.124
Here's what sources close to former

00:03:11.124 --> 00:03:12.158
President Trump are saying.

00:03:12.158 --> 00:03:13.159
They're saying that

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:14.460
he was just asking

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.729
his lawyer, Corcoran, for legal advice

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:18.131
whether when he asked about

00:03:18.131 --> 00:03:18.965
whether or not

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:20.200
they could fight the subpoena.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.035
So if you're a prosecutor

00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:23.469
and you're examining these notes,

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:24.437
how do you determine

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:27.473
what is the line between perhaps Trump

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:28.341
trying to obstruct

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:29.142
justice, asking

00:03:29.142 --> 00:03:30.843
how to get out of a subpoena?

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:31.844
And Trump,

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:32.378
you know,

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:34.080
let's let's let's us

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.515
play devil's advocate.

00:03:35.515 --> 00:03:36.849
Trump could have been playing devil's

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:37.984
advocate in that moment.

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:39.485
I think that is what his

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:41.821
his aides are suggesting here.

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:44.657
Well, as I piece together the reporting,

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:46.359
it appears what might have happened

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:47.460
is he might have

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.529
legitimately probed his lawyer,

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:50.463
but the lawyer

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:52.165
but he took the advice

00:03:52.165 --> 00:03:52.665
his lawyer

00:03:52.665 --> 00:03:54.167
gave him and turned around

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:55.935
and shared it with somebody else.

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:58.271
And they appear to have moved documents

00:03:58.271 --> 00:03:59.706
and things of that nature.

00:03:59.706 --> 00:04:00.673
Once the subpoena

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:03.042
arrived to try to avoid it

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:05.345
being fully uncovered and discovered

00:04:05.745 --> 00:04:06.913
So that's the sort of thing

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:08.681
that these notes can tell us

00:04:08.681 --> 00:04:10.583
and lead us to

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:11.985
have a better understanding of.

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:14.420
And that would show his criminal intent.

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:15.121
You know,

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:17.390
whether or not it's just willful

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:19.892
use of this material

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:22.028
or whether it's an obstruction,

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:23.663
it appears the obstruction case

00:04:23.663 --> 00:04:25.832
is most prominent and strongest

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:26.799
at this point.

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:28.501
So there's another detail

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:30.270
that is very interesting

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:30.737
that we're learning

00:04:30.737 --> 00:04:31.571
from The New York Times.

00:04:31.571 --> 00:04:33.072
They're reporting that prosecutors

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:33.973
have also issued

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:34.841
a subpoena

00:04:34.841 --> 00:04:37.610
about Trump's foreign businesses in seven

00:04:37.744 --> 00:04:39.078
very specific countries

00:04:39.078 --> 00:04:39.779
in China,

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:40.913
France, Turkey,

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:42.482
Saudi Arabia, Kuwait

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:43.950
and the United Arab Emirates.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:46.052
And also Oman.

00:04:46.052 --> 00:04:46.986
What does

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:48.221
does it say to you

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:49.922
that they are looking at these

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:53.426
deals, deals that date back to 2017,

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:56.462
meaning wild Trump was still president of

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:57.330
the United States?

00:04:58.431 --> 00:04:59.565
Well, it's

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:00.099
in fact

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:00.266
that it

00:05:00.266 --> 00:05:00.700
goes back

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.835
throughout his presidency is very telling

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:05.638
that they're looking to see

00:05:05.638 --> 00:05:08.641
what he might have shared.

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:09.242
And I think there's

00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:10.743
a good reason to do that.

00:05:10.743 --> 00:05:13.279
What he shared of intelligence nature

00:05:13.513 --> 00:05:14.414
we know he did it

00:05:14.414 --> 00:05:15.682
well in the Oval Office

00:05:15.682 --> 00:05:16.649
and they had to rush

00:05:16.649 --> 00:05:19.052
declassify information when he gave

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:22.755
Ambassador Lavrov

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:24.991
clearly sources and methods

00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:27.093
which was a troublesome thing.

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:28.594
But here

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:31.064
you know I thought my immediate reaction

00:05:31.064 --> 00:05:33.866
when Kaitlan asked him at the town hall

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:34.934
you know

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:35.902
have you ever shared

00:05:35.902 --> 00:05:38.338
any of this information with anybody?

00:05:38.338 --> 00:05:40.273
The answer that most people

00:05:40.273 --> 00:05:42.475
would have given was, of course I didn't.

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:44.510
This was national security information.

00:05:44.911 --> 00:05:47.580
Trump's answer was, I don't recall.

00:05:47.947 --> 00:05:50.583
That just doesn't flip.

00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:51.784
It's not surprising

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:53.419
that the special counsel

00:05:53.419 --> 00:05:54.687
is trying to find out

00:05:54.687 --> 00:05:55.221
who in the world

00:05:55.221 --> 00:05:56.889
was this man dealing with

00:05:56.889 --> 00:05:58.925
and what might have been

00:05:58.925 --> 00:05:59.692
an occasion

00:05:59.692 --> 00:06:00.159
that he could have

00:06:00.159 --> 00:06:01.427
shared this information

00:06:01.427 --> 00:06:03.629
or what motive might have been

00:06:03.963 --> 00:06:05.098
for the information?

00:06:05.098 --> 00:06:05.298
Yeah.

00:06:05.298 --> 00:06:05.465
I mean,

00:06:05.465 --> 00:06:07.600
I think that speaks to a major question

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:08.401
that we still have,

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:09.769
which is the why of it all.

00:06:09.769 --> 00:06:12.372
Why would he want to keep the documents?

00:06:12.372 --> 00:06:14.307
What is the motive, as you just said?

00:06:14.307 --> 00:06:15.074
But turning

00:06:15.074 --> 00:06:16.743
to one of the other legal cases

00:06:16.743 --> 00:06:19.045
that the former president

00:06:19.045 --> 00:06:19.912
has been embroiled

00:06:19.912 --> 00:06:22.348
in, this is dealing with AG and Carroll's

00:06:22.915 --> 00:06:23.950
defamation

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:26.252
and sexual assault case against him.

00:06:26.853 --> 00:06:30.156
It seems now that she is wanting

00:06:30.156 --> 00:06:30.990
to amend

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:32.959
this case based on his comments

00:06:32.959 --> 00:06:34.460
in that CNN town hall.

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:35.995
I want you to take a listen to this

00:06:38.531 --> 00:06:40.199
They said he didn't rape her

00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:40.733
and they didn't

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:41.868
I didn't do anything else either.

00:06:41.868 --> 00:06:42.201
You know what?

00:06:42.201 --> 00:06:42.969
Because I have no idea

00:06:42.969 --> 00:06:43.870
who the hell she is.

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:45.538
But, Mr. President, can I ask.

00:06:45.538 --> 00:06:47.306
They said, sir, don't do it.

00:06:47.306 --> 00:06:48.608
This is a fake story,

00:06:48.608 --> 00:06:49.642
and you don't want to give it

00:06:49.642 --> 00:06:50.343
credibility.

00:06:50.343 --> 00:06:51.511
One thing you go

00:06:51.511 --> 00:06:53.880
one thing you did do in this.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:56.783
And I swear and I've never done that.

00:06:56.783 --> 00:06:59.252
And I swear to I have no idea

00:06:59.252 --> 00:07:01.120
who the hell she's a

00:07:02.855 --> 00:07:03.956
she's a whack job.

00:07:03.956 --> 00:07:05.792
So what do you make of today's filings?

00:07:05.792 --> 00:07:07.827
Are you surprised at all?

00:07:07.927 --> 00:07:08.828
Not at all.

00:07:08.828 --> 00:07:09.929
I think that

00:07:09.929 --> 00:07:12.565
what was done was very thoughtful.

00:07:13.533 --> 00:07:14.567
It wasn't a new case.

00:07:14.567 --> 00:07:15.635
It was filed

00:07:15.635 --> 00:07:16.536
it was filed against

00:07:16.536 --> 00:07:17.937
the original complaint

00:07:17.937 --> 00:07:21.374
that was done back in November of 2019.

00:07:21.707 --> 00:07:23.042
That has been bouncing

00:07:23.042 --> 00:07:24.577
around the courts over

00:07:24.577 --> 00:07:25.912
who can represent Trump,

00:07:25.912 --> 00:07:27.647
whether he because he was president

00:07:27.647 --> 00:07:28.681
when he said that

00:07:28.681 --> 00:07:29.882
the Department of Justice

00:07:29.882 --> 00:07:31.417
should be involved in this.

00:07:31.417 --> 00:07:32.885
And that has not been.

00:07:32.885 --> 00:07:35.087
It's gone up to two court of appeals

00:07:35.087 --> 00:07:36.088
and now it's back down

00:07:36.088 --> 00:07:37.323
in the district court.

00:07:37.323 --> 00:07:38.524
That's where she amended it.

00:07:38.524 --> 00:07:39.559
It's back there

00:07:39.559 --> 00:07:41.594
and it shows punitive damages.

00:07:41.894 --> 00:07:44.030
It many of these issues

00:07:44.030 --> 00:07:45.364
in the original case

00:07:45.364 --> 00:07:46.799
have already been tried.

00:07:46.799 --> 00:07:49.135
It's the same judge. He's very savvy.

00:07:49.135 --> 00:07:50.937
He knows what's going on.

00:07:50.937 --> 00:07:52.705
It was a brilliant move.

00:07:52.705 --> 00:07:54.407
And I think Trump could end up

00:07:54.407 --> 00:07:55.842
paying another five

00:07:55.842 --> 00:07:57.443
